#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Zoom training-session attendance monitor - v1 (advisory only).

Receives Zoom event-subscription webhooks, tracks cumulative absence per
participant against the 30-minute rule, evaluates waiting-room arrivals
against an uploaded eligibility sheet (CSV) and a manual exclusion list,
and shows a live status page with alerts.

Takes NO actions inside Zoom. It watches and advises; the human decides.

Stdlib only. Run: python3 app.py

Config via environment variables:
  PORT                  default 8080
  ZOOM_SECRET_TOKEN     Secret Token from the Zoom Marketplace webhook app.
                        Required in production (used for endpoint validation
                        and request signature checks). Empty = accept all
                        POSTs (local testing only; a warning is logged).
  ABSENCE_LIMIT_MINUTES default 30  (the 30-minute rule)
  LATE_ALERT_MINUTES    default 10  (joining after this flags a late alert)
  DB_PATH               default attendance.db
"""

